From cbe7ad96ba63f2147c4ca13f34e74f783fad11f7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 08:14:50 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/5] Add .gitignore, a README and a GitHub Actions build check

- .gitignore keeps build output, local.properties, UI dumps, patch and bundle
  files out of the repo
- a GitHub Actions job runs ./gradlew assembleDebug on every push and keeps
  the APK, so a broken build is noticed immediately
- shorter README with the build steps
---
 .github/workflows/build.yml | 22 ++++++++++++++++++++
 .gitignore                  | 15 ++++++++++++++
 README.md                   | 40 ++++++++++++++++++-------------------
 3 files changed, 56 insertions(+), 21 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 .github/workflows/build.yml
 create mode 100644 .gitignore

diff --git a/.github/workflows/build.yml b/.github/workflows/build.yml
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..2bc51ec
--- /dev/null
+++ b/.github/workflows/build.yml
@@ -0,0 +1,22 @@
+name: build
+
+on:
+  push:
+  pull_request:
+
+jobs:
+  debug-apk:
+    runs-on: ubuntu-latest
+    steps:
+      - uses: actions/checkout@v4
+      - uses: actions/setup-java@v4
+        with:
+          distribution: temurin
+          java-version: 17
+      - name: Build debug APK
+        run: ./gradlew assembleDebug --no-daemon
+      - name: Keep the APK
+        uses: actions/upload-artifact@v4
+        with:
+          name: swizy-debug-apk
+          path: app/build/outputs/apk/debug/app-debug.apk
diff --git a/.gitignore b/.gitignore
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..0692e99
--- /dev/null
+++ b/.gitignore
@@ -0,0 +1,15 @@
+# build output and local machine settings
+.gradle/
+build/
+local.properties
+.idea/
+*.iml
+.cxx/
+captures/
+*.apk
+
+# debugging leftovers: UI dumps contain on-screen text, patch/bundle files are not source
+window.xml
+output*.txt
+*.patch
+*.bundle
diff --git a/README.md b/README.md
index 79986eb..27e2a2c 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -1,26 +1,24 @@
 # swizy
 
-An Android privacy utility with Lowery avatar masking, manual per-app layouts,
-Sibha counting, and offline-capable prayer times.
+A small Android app (Kotlin, no dependencies) with a few personal tools:
 
-Lowery also includes **Hide an area manually**. Summon the app-icon ball from
-the Lowery tab, open its menu, choose **Add**, and drag across any screen
-region. Multiple rectangles remain black independently of avatar detection.
-The movable ball fades while idle and provides Add, remove-last, show/hide-all,
-move-boxes, and Close controls. Settings also has **Do nothing (manual only)**,
-which disables dynamic avatar detection while leaving manual boxes available.
-Choose **Add profile** from the ball to capture boxes for the current foreground
-app, then choose **Save profile**. Saved profiles apply automatically when that
-app returns to the foreground; profiles can also be reviewed and managed in
-Settings.
+- **Lowery**: an accessibility service that covers profile pictures in WhatsApp, Telegram
+  and LinkedIn with one vertical line (or circles), plus manual black boxes and per-app profiles.
+  Toggle it from the app or the Quick Settings tile.
+- **Sibha**: a tap counter with an optional beep and vibration every N counts.
+- **Prayers**: daily prayer times from aladhan.com (GPS or manual coordinates), cached offline.
+- **Headset time**: long-press the button on wired headphones to hear the time.
 
-Release settings include app/orientation profiles, undo/redo, JSON layout
-backup, optional privacy indicator, battery saver scanning, mask color/opacity,
-and a local crash log.
-Optional headset time filters a long press of a wired headset media button,
-announces the current time, then resumes music that was playing. Short presses
-are passed through normally.
+## Build
 
-See [`PROJECT_PATHS.md`](PROJECT_PATHS.md) for the module layout and build/install
-commands. The supplied patch references and combined review bundle are kept under
-[`patches/`](patches/).
+```
+./gradlew assembleDebug
+adb install -r app/build/outputs/apk/debug/app-debug.apk
+```
+
+Needs JDK 17 and the Android SDK (`sdk.dir` in `local.properties`, which is not tracked).
+Every push is also built by GitHub Actions; the APK is attached to each run.
+After installing, enable **swizy** under Settings > Accessibility.
+
+Code: `MainActivity.kt` (screens), `AvatarService.kt` (masking, boxes, headset),
+`Prefs.kt` (settings storage), `BlackoutTile.kt` (Quick Settings tile).
